course: dictionary
lesson: 6905
title: Animal words and similes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An ox is a big, strong farm animal, like a bull. Farmers used oxen to pull carts and ploughs. Read the words around ox to see what it is doing. «The Ox came with the yoke on his neck to plough.» A yoke is a wooden bar for pulling, and ploughing is work in the fields, so this ox is a working farm animal.
explain: The plural of ox is oxen, not oxes. «As strong as an ox» is a simile, a comparison that tells you something is very strong. You do not need a real ox to understand it, because the words around it show the meaning.
explain: Look at this sentence: «When wolves come, musk oxen stand in a ring with the calves in the middle and their horns pointing out.» Wolves, calves, ring and horns pointing out all show that the oxen are protecting their young. Ask yourself what word would fit, then check it in the sentence.
fact: Ox is a noun. Its plural is oxen.
fact: «Ox» means a big, strong farm animal like a bull, used to pull carts and ploughs.
fact: «As strong as an ox» means very strong.
fact: In the Chinese zodiac, the ox comes second, after the rat and before the tiger.
fact: The zodiac animals repeat in a 12-year cycle, so the ox comes back every 12 years; the link to character is tradition and fun, not science.
exercise: «The Ox came with the yoke on his neck to plough.» What job was the ox doing? | Singing for the farmer | Swimming across a river | *Pulling a plough in the fields | Carrying a child to school
exercise: What does «as strong as an ox» mean? | *Very strong | Very far away | Very weak | Very tired
exercise: What is the plural of ox? | *oxen | oxies | oxes
test: Which animal comes between the rat and the tiger in the Chinese zodiac? | *ox | rabbit | dragon
test: What does an ox do on a farm? | *Pulls carts and ploughs | Swims in the sea | Lays eggs | Flies over the fields
exam: In «When wolves come, musk oxen stand in a ring with the calves in the middle», why do the oxen form a ring? | To sleep in the sun | *To keep the calves safe from wolves | To find food | To dance together
